    "body": "Jennifer and team,\n\nLet me provide the vendor perspective on feasible options and associated costs/timelines:\n\n**Option 1: Expedited Capacity Addition**\n• Timeline: 6 weeks to recruit, credential, and certify 2 additional cardiologists\n• Cost: $125K setup fee + $850/read (vs. current $650/read contract rate)\n• Impact: Returns to 5-day SLA by early January, maintains quality standards\n• Risk: Tight timeline over holiday period, dependent on successful recruitment\n\n**Option 2: Study Prioritization with Existing Capacity**\n• Prioritize NCT00542451 ECHOs for 3-day expedited reads\n• Other portfolio studies move to 14-day turnaround  \n• Cost: No additional fees, within current contract\n• Impact: Meets NCT00542451 timeline, but delays other studies by ~2 weeks\n\n**Option 3: Hybrid Approach**  \n• Prioritize NCT00542451 for 3-day reads through January\n• Add capacity starting in January for portfolio normalization\n• Cost: $75K setup fee + $750/read for incremental volume\n• Impact: Protects NCT00542451 IA, minimizes other study delays\n\n**Impact Analysis by Study (Option 2 - Prioritization):**\n• NCT00542462: Database lock delay from March 15 to April 1 (impacts Q2 submission)\n• NCT00542475: Enrollment ongoing, affects real-time safety monitoring\n• Two other studies: Minimal impact, earlier in enrollment phase\n\n**Recommendation:** Option 3 provides best risk/benefit balance - protects the interim analysis while adding permanent capacity to prevent future bottlenecks.\n\nHowever, I want to flag: any of these options require change order approval, and we're already at 95% of our contracted volume for FY2025. Additional capacity may trigger contract renegotiation.\n\nSarah - this needs decision by November 27 to implement in time for January timeline. Beyond that date, we cannot guarantee the interim analysis deadline even with expedited approach.\n\nPlease let me know how you'd like to proceed.\n\nBest regards,\n\nDavid Chen, PhD\nDirector, C